IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `dg-core`
IMPORT `dg7-governing-provisions`
IMPORT `dg7-nonstock-mergers`
IMPORT `dg7-merger-effects`
IMPORT `dg7-appraisal-rights`
IMPORT `dg7-appraisal-procedure`
IMPORT `dg7-appraisal-proceeding`
IMPORT `dg7-seat`

-- Worked cases for dg7-seat.l4: one case or more for every question, in the facts a real person in the seat would state.
-- Every expected value is decided here from the text of ss 255 to 262, not from the code's output. Each case says in a comment what the
-- person is asking and why the answer is what it is.

§ `Section 255: nonstock corporations of this State`

-- Two Delaware nonprofit corporations, a merger into one of them, and the agreement is approved: they may merge.
#ASSERT `May our nonstock corporations merge or consolidate under section 255` 2 2 FALSE TRUE FALSE TRUE
-- Three corporations, but only two are Delaware nonstock corporations: the third is not within section 255.
#ASSERT NOT (`May our nonstock corporations merge or consolidate under section 255` 3 2 FALSE TRUE FALSE TRUE)
-- A consolidation into a new nonstock corporation.
#ASSERT `May our nonstock corporations merge or consolidate under section 255` 2 2 TRUE FALSE TRUE TRUE
-- A consolidation into a new stock corporation is not a consolidation "into a new resulting nonstock corporation".
#ASSERT NOT (`May our nonstock corporations merge or consolidate under section 255` 2 2 TRUE FALSE FALSE TRUE)
-- The agreement has not been approved as the section requires.
#ASSERT NOT (`May our nonstock corporations merge or consolidate under section 255` 2 2 FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE)
-- A single corporation cannot merge with itself under the section: "2 or more".
#ASSERT NOT (`May our nonstock corporations merge or consolidate under section 255` 1 1 FALSE TRUE FALSE TRUE)

-- Our merger agreement states the terms, the mode, that the certificate stays as it is, how memberships convert, and what the holders of
-- the memberships that do not remain outstanding receive; no cash in place of fractions.
#ASSERT `Does our merger agreement state what section 255(b) requires` FALSE TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE
-- It leaves out what the holders of the cancelled memberships will receive.
#ASSERT NOT (`Does our merger agreement state what section 255(b) requires` FALSE TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE)
-- A consolidation whose agreement does not say that the new certificate is attached.
#ASSERT NOT (`Does our merger agreement state what section 255(b) requires` TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE)
-- The same consolidation agreement with the attachment statement.
#ASSERT `Does our merger agreement state what section 255(b) requires` TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE
-- Cash in place of fractions that is not consistent with section 155.
#ASSERT NOT (`Does our merger agreement state what section 255(b) requires` FALSE TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE)

-- Executed by an authorized person and filed in the form of section 103.
#ASSERT `Is our merger agreement properly executed` TRUE TRUE TRUE
-- Filed, but not executed and acknowledged as section 103 requires.
#ASSERT NOT (`Is our merger agreement properly executed` TRUE TRUE FALSE)
-- A certificate of merger is filed in its place, so the agreement itself is not filed.
#ASSERT `Is our merger agreement properly executed` TRUE FALSE FALSE

-- A term (the price) depends on an index published elsewhere, and the agreement sets out how the index operates on the price.
#ASSERT `May a term of our merger agreement depend on facts outside the agreement` TRUE
#ASSERT NOT (`May a term of our merger agreement depend on facts outside the agreement` FALSE)

-- "Facts" includes an event, a determination and an action; for anything else the sentence does not say.
#ASSERT `Is this a fact on which a term of our merger agreement may depend` `the occurrence of an event` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Is this a fact on which a term of our merger agreement may depend` `a determination by a person or body, including the corporation` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Is this a fact on which a term of our merger agreement may depend` `an action by a person or body, including the corporation` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Is this a fact on which a term of our merger agreement may depend` `something that is neither an event, a determination nor an action` EQUALS NOTHING

-- A member with a vote for the governing body is owed notice of the meeting.
#ASSERT `Must I, as a member, be given notice of the meeting on the merger` TRUE FALSE
-- A member without that vote but entitled to vote on the merger under the bylaws.
#ASSERT `Must I, as a member, be given notice of the meeting on the merger` FALSE TRUE
-- A member with neither vote.
#ASSERT NOT (`Must I, as a member, be given notice of the meeting on the merger` FALSE FALSE)

-- The meeting is on 20 May 2026: the notice must be given by 30 April 2026.
#ASSERT `By what date must notice of the meeting on the merger be given to me` (YearMonthDay 2026 5 20) EQUALS YearMonthDay 2026 4 30
-- The meeting is on 15 March 2026: 20 days earlier is 23 February 2026 (February 2026 has 28 days).
#ASSERT `By what date must notice of the meeting on the merger be given to me` (YearMonthDay 2026 3 15) EQUALS YearMonthDay 2026 2 23

-- The notice I got on 30 April for the 20 May meeting states time, place and purpose, has a summary and my address.
#ASSERT `Is the notice of the meeting I received good enough` (YearMonthDay 2026 4 30) (YearMonthDay 2026 5 20) TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE TRUE TRUE
-- The notice I got on 1 May for the 20 May meeting is 19 days before.
#ASSERT NOT (`Is the notice of the meeting I received good enough` (YearMonthDay 2026 5 1) (YearMonthDay 2026 5 20) TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE TRUE TRUE)
-- A notice with neither a copy nor a summary.
#ASSERT NOT (`Is the notice of the meeting I received good enough` (YearMonthDay 2026 4 1) (YearMonthDay 2026 5 20) TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE TRUE)
-- A notice sent to an address not on the corporation's records.
#ASSERT NOT (`Is the notice of the meeting I received good enough` (YearMonthDay 2026 4 1) (YearMonthDay 2026 5 20) TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE)

-- 60 members entitled to vote, 31 voted for: a majority of all of them.
#ASSERT `Have the members adopted the merger agreement` 60 31 EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- 30 of 60 is half, not a majority.
#ASSERT `Have the members adopted the merger agreement` 60 30 EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- Not covered: no members are entitled to vote.
#ASSERT `Have the members adopted the merger agreement` 0 0 EQUALS NOTHING

-- The secretary's officer certified it on the agreement.
#ASSERT `Has the adoption been certified on the agreement as it must be` TRUE FALSE
-- No certification, but a certificate of merger is filed in place of the agreement.
#ASSERT `Has the adoption been certified on the agreement as it must be` FALSE TRUE
-- No certification and the agreement itself is filed.
#ASSERT NOT (`Has the adoption been certified on the agreement as it must be` FALSE FALSE)

-- Our corporation has no member who votes except the 5 members of the governing body, and 3 of them adopted the resolution.
#ASSERT `Can our governing body approve the merger on its own` TRUE 5 3 EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- Only 2 of the 5.
#ASSERT `Can our governing body approve the merger on its own` TRUE 5 2 EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- Other members have a vote, so the governing body cannot approve on its own.
#ASSERT `Can our governing body approve the merger on its own` FALSE 5 5 EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- Not covered: no members of the governing body are counted.
#ASSERT `Can our governing body approve the merger on its own` TRUE 0 0 EQUALS NOTHING

-- Our corporation: resolution adopted, 80 members entitled to vote and 50 voted for, the secretary's officer certified it.
#ASSERT `Has our corporation approved the merger agreement as section 255 requires` TRUE FALSE 7 7 80 50 TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- 40 of 80 voted for: not a majority.
#ASSERT `Has our corporation approved the merger agreement as section 255 requires` TRUE FALSE 7 7 80 40 TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- The governing body alone (subsection (d)): 4 of 7 adopted, certified.
#ASSERT `Has our corporation approved the merger agreement as section 255 requires` FALSE TRUE 7 4 0 0 TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- Not covered: no members to count.
#ASSERT `Has our corporation approved the merger agreement as section 255 requires` TRUE FALSE 7 7 0 0 TRUE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING

-- When the filing becomes effective under section 103 (1 September 2026), once each corporation has adopted and certified.
#ASSERT `When does our merger become effective` TRUE (YearMonthDay 2026 9 1) EQUALS JUST (YearMonthDay 2026 9 1)
-- One corporation has not yet adopted and certified: not effective.
#ASSERT `When does our merger become effective` FALSE (YearMonthDay 2026 9 1) EQUALS NOTHING

-- A member is a stockholder for the certificate-of-merger provisions (so may ask for a copy of the agreement without cost).
#ASSERT `Am I, as a member, treated as a stockholder for the certificate-of-merger provisions of section 251(c)` FALSE TRUE
#ASSERT NOT (`Am I, as a member, treated as a stockholder for the certificate-of-merger provisions of section 251(c)` FALSE FALSE)

-- Section 255 brings in the last sentence of s 251(c), s 251(d) and s 251(e), not s 251(f).
#ASSERT `Does this provision of section 251 apply to our merger under section 255` `s 251(d), terminating or amending the agreement before it becomes effective`
#ASSERT `Does this provision of section 251 apply to our merger under section 255` `s 251(e), the automatic amendment of the surviving corporation's certificate of incorporation`
#ASSERT `Does this provision of section 251 apply to our merger under section 255` `the last sentence of s 251(c), a certificate of merger or consolidation in lieu of filing the agreement`
#ASSERT NOT (`Does this provision of section 251 apply to our merger under section 255` `s 251(f), no vote of the stockholders of a constituent corporation surviving a merger`)

-- The word "stockholders" in section 251(d) is read as "members" for our nonstock corporation.
#ASSERT `How is this reference in section 251(d) read for our nonstock corporation` `a reference to stockholders` EQUALS `a reference to members of the corporation`
#ASSERT `How is this reference in section 251(d) read for our nonstock corporation` `a reference to the board of directors` EQUALS `a reference to the governing body of the corporation`

-- A charitable nonstock corporation merged into a non-charitable nonstock corporation, losing its charitable status: section 255 does not authorize it.
#ASSERT `Does section 255 forbid our merger because a charitable nonstock corporation would lose its charitable status` FALSE `a charitable nonstock corporation` `a nonprofit nonstock corporation that is not charitable` TRUE
-- The charitable status would not be lost or impaired.
#ASSERT NOT (`Does section 255 forbid our merger because a charitable nonstock corporation would lose its charitable status` FALSE `a charitable nonstock corporation` `a nonprofit nonstock corporation that is not charitable` FALSE)
-- A nonstock corporation may be merged into our charitable nonstock corporation, which survives.
#ASSERT `May a nonstock corporation be merged into our charitable nonstock corporation that survives` `a nonprofit nonstock corporation that is not charitable` `a charitable nonstock corporation`
-- Not if the surviving corporation is not charitable.
#ASSERT NOT (`May a nonstock corporation be merged into our charitable nonstock corporation that survives` `a nonprofit nonstock corporation that is not charitable` `a nonprofit nonstock corporation that is not charitable`)

§ `Section 256: domestic and foreign nonstock corporations`

-- One Delaware nonstock corporation and one foreign nonstock corporation, a merger into one of them, the foreign law does not prohibit it.
#ASSERT `May our Delaware nonstock corporation merge or consolidate with a foreign nonstock corporation` 1 1 0 FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE TRUE
-- The foreign law prohibits the merger: "unless the laws of the jurisdiction ... prohibit".
#ASSERT NOT (`May our Delaware nonstock corporation merge or consolidate with a foreign nonstock corporation` 1 1 0 FALSE TRUE FALSE TRUE TRUE)
-- Two Delaware nonstock corporations and no foreign one: that is section 255, not section 256.
#ASSERT NOT (`May our Delaware nonstock corporation merge or consolidate with a foreign nonstock corporation` 2 0 0 FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE TRUE)
-- A third, stock, corporation is taking part: not within section 256.
#ASSERT NOT (`May our Delaware nonstock corporation merge or consolidate with a foreign nonstock corporation` 1 1 1 FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE TRUE)
-- A consolidation into a new nonstock corporation of the jurisdiction of one of them.
#ASSERT `May our Delaware nonstock corporation merge or consolidate with a foreign nonstock corporation` 1 1 0 TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE TRUE

-- A nonprofit nonstock corporation organized in another State is a foreign nonstock corporation.
#ASSERT `Is this corporation a foreign nonstock corporation` `a nonprofit nonstock corporation that is not charitable` `another jurisdiction of the United States`
-- A stock corporation is not.
#ASSERT NOT (`Is this corporation a foreign nonstock corporation` `a stock corporation` `a foreign jurisdiction outside the United States`)
-- A Delaware nonstock corporation is not "foreign".
#ASSERT NOT (`Is this corporation a foreign nonstock corporation` `a charitable nonstock corporation` `this State`)

-- The agreement: all entered into it, the survivor is a Delaware corporation, terms, mode, amendments, memberships converted, the manner,
-- some do not remain outstanding, what they receive, no cash in place of fractions, and what the foreign law requires.
#ASSERT `Does the merger agreement state what section 256(b) requires` TRUE TRUE FALSE TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE TRUE
-- It omits what the foreign law requires.
#ASSERT NOT (`Does the merger agreement state what section 256(b) requires` TRUE TRUE FALSE TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE)
-- The survivor is not a Delaware corporation: items (3) and (4) do not bite, so no amendments statement is needed.
#ASSERT `Does the merger agreement state what section 256(b) requires` TRUE FALSE FALSE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE
-- Not every constituent corporation entered into the agreement.
#ASSERT NOT (`Does the merger agreement state what section 256(b) requires` FALSE TRUE FALSE TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE TRUE)

-- A Delaware constituent: its own law and the manner of section 255.
#ASSERT `Has this constituent corporation approved the agreement as section 256(c) requires` `this State` TRUE TRUE
#ASSERT NOT (`Has this constituent corporation approved the agreement as section 256(c) requires` `this State` TRUE FALSE)
-- A foreign constituent: its own law only.
#ASSERT `Has this constituent corporation approved the agreement as section 256(c) requires` `another jurisdiction of the United States` TRUE FALSE
#ASSERT NOT (`Has this constituent corporation approved the agreement as section 256(c) requires` `another jurisdiction of the United States` FALSE TRUE)

-- Section 256 brings in the last sentence of s 252(c) and s 251(d); s 251(e) only where the survivor is a Delaware corporation; not s 251(f).
#ASSERT `Does this provision of section 251 or 252 apply to our merger under section 256` `the last sentence of s 252(c), a certificate of merger or consolidation in lieu of filing the agreement` FALSE
#ASSERT `Does this provision of section 251 or 252 apply to our merger under section 256` `s 251(d), terminating or amending the agreement before it becomes effective` FALSE
#ASSERT `Does this provision of section 251 or 252 apply to our merger under section 256` `s 251(e), the automatic amendment of the surviving corporation's certificate of incorporation` TRUE
#ASSERT NOT (`Does this provision of section 251 or 252 apply to our merger under section 256` `s 251(e), the automatic amendment of the surviving corporation's certificate of incorporation` FALSE)
#ASSERT NOT (`Does this provision of section 251 or 252 apply to our merger under section 256` `s 251(f), no vote of the stockholders of a constituent corporation surviving a merger` TRUE)

-- Our surviving foreign nonstock corporation agreed to be served in Delaware, irrevocably appointed the Secretary of State, and gave an address.
#ASSERT `Has our surviving foreign nonstock corporation done what section 256(d) requires of it` TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE
-- It gave no address.
#ASSERT NOT (`Has our surviving foreign nonstock corporation done what section 256(d) requires of it` TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE)
-- The appointment is not irrevocable.
#ASSERT NOT (`Has our surviving foreign nonstock corporation done what section 256(d) requires of it` TRUE TRUE FALSE TRUE)
-- The survivor is not a foreign nonstock corporation: the subsection asks nothing of it.
#ASSERT `Has our surviving foreign nonstock corporation done what section 256(d) requires of it` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE

-- I served by e-mail in the way the Secretary of State prescribes.
#ASSERT `Is my electronic service of process on the Secretary of State good` TRUE TRUE
-- I served by e-mail but not as prescribed.
#ASSERT NOT (`Is my electronic service of process on the Secretary of State good` TRUE FALSE)
-- I served on paper.
#ASSERT `Is my electronic service of process on the Secretary of State good` FALSE FALSE

-- As plaintiff I served in duplicate, told the Secretary of State and paid the fee.
#ASSERT `Have I done what section 256(d) requires of a plaintiff serving through the Secretary of State` TRUE TRUE TRUE
-- I did not pay the fee.
#ASSERT NOT (`Have I done what section 256(d) requires of a plaintiff serving through the Secretary of State` TRUE TRUE FALSE)
-- I served only one copy.
#ASSERT NOT (`Have I done what section 256(d) requires of a plaintiff serving through the Secretary of State` FALSE TRUE TRUE)

-- I paid the fee and I won: the fee is taxed as part of the costs.
#ASSERT `Will the fee I paid the Secretary of State be taxed as part of the costs` TRUE TRUE
-- I lost.
#ASSERT NOT (`Will the fee I paid the Secretary of State be taxed as part of the costs` TRUE FALSE)

-- The Secretary of State mails to the address specified, or to the last address designated in writing.
#ASSERT `To what address must the Secretary of State mail the letter to our corporation` "1 Main Street, Wilmington" FALSE "" EQUALS "1 Main Street, Wilmington"
#ASSERT `To what address must the Secretary of State mail the letter to our corporation` "1 Main Street, Wilmington" TRUE "9 Side Street, Dover" EQUALS "9 Side Street, Dover"

-- The letter was sent forthwith, by a mail or courier service with the records, enclosing the papers, to the right address.
#ASSERT `Was the Secretary of State's letter to our corporation sent as section 256(d) requires` TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE
-- It did not enclose a copy of the process.
#ASSERT NOT (`Was the Secretary of State's letter to our corporation sent as section 256(d) requires` TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE TRUE)
-- It was not sent forthwith.
#ASSERT NOT (`Was the Secretary of State's letter to our corporation sent as section 256(d) requires` FALSE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE)

-- The service was received on 1 March 2026. The Secretary of State need not keep the record longer than 5 years from receipt.
#ASSERT `Can the Secretary of State now discard the record of the service` (YearMonthDay 2026 3 1) (YearMonthDay 2031 3 2)
#ASSERT NOT (`Can the Secretary of State now discard the record of the service` (YearMonthDay 2026 3 1) (YearMonthDay 2031 3 1))

-- A charitable nonstock corporation merged into another nonstock corporation, losing its charitable status: not authorized by section 256.
#ASSERT `Does section 256 forbid our merger because a charitable nonstock corporation would lose its charitable status` FALSE `a charitable nonstock corporation` `a nonstock corporation with membership interests` TRUE

§ `Section 257: stock corporations with nonstock corporations of this State`

-- One Delaware nonstock and one Delaware stock corporation.
#ASSERT `May our Delaware nonstock and stock corporations merge or consolidate under section 257` 1 1 0 TRUE
-- Two nonstock corporations: that is section 255.
#ASSERT NOT (`May our Delaware nonstock and stock corporations merge or consolidate under section 257` 2 0 0 TRUE)
-- A third corporation, of another jurisdiction.
#ASSERT NOT (`May our Delaware nonstock and stock corporations merge or consolidate under section 257` 1 1 1 TRUE)
-- The agreement is not approved as the section requires.
#ASSERT NOT (`May our Delaware nonstock and stock corporations merge or consolidate under section 257` 1 1 0 FALSE)

-- The survivor may be a nonstock corporation, or a stock corporation.
#ASSERT `May the surviving or resulting corporation be of this kind` `a nonstock corporation with membership interests`
#ASSERT `May the surviving or resulting corporation be of this kind` `a stock corporation`

-- The resolution is adopted by the board of directors of a stock corporation and the governing body of a nonstock corporation.
#ASSERT `Which body must adopt the resolution approving the agreement for my corporation` `a stock corporation` EQUALS `the board of directors`
#ASSERT `Which body must adopt the resolution approving the agreement for my corporation` `a nonprofit nonstock corporation that is not charitable` EQUALS `the governing body`

-- A merger agreement that states everything, including how certificates are surrendered.
#ASSERT `Does the merger agreement state what section 257(b) requires` FALSE TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE
-- Shares do not remain outstanding but the agreement does not state the surrender of certificates.
#ASSERT NOT (`Does the merger agreement state what section 257(b) requires` FALSE TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE)

-- A stock corporation approves in the manner of section 251; a nonstock corporation in the manner of section 255.
#ASSERT `In the manner of which section must my corporation approve the merger agreement` `a stock corporation` EQUALS `s 251, the section on stock corporations`
#ASSERT `In the manner of which section must my corporation approve the merger agreement` `a charitable nonstock corporation` EQUALS `s 255, the section on nonstock corporations`

-- Section 257 brings in s 251(f) for a constituent stock corporation in a merger, not in a consolidation.
#ASSERT `Does this provision of section 251 or 252 apply to our merger under section 257` `s 251(f), no vote of the stockholders of a constituent corporation surviving a merger` TRUE TRUE
#ASSERT NOT (`Does this provision of section 251 or 252 apply to our merger under section 257` `s 251(f), no vote of the stockholders of a constituent corporation surviving a merger` FALSE TRUE)
#ASSERT `Does this provision of section 251 or 252 apply to our merger under section 257` `s 251(d), terminating or amending the agreement before it becomes effective` TRUE FALSE

-- A charitable nonstock corporation merged into a stock corporation with its charitable status lost: not authorized.
#ASSERT `Does section 257 forbid our merger because a charitable nonstock corporation would lose its charitable status` FALSE `a charitable nonstock corporation` `a stock corporation` TRUE
-- A stock corporation may be merged into our charitable nonstock corporation, which survives.
#ASSERT `May a stock corporation be merged into our charitable nonstock corporation that survives` `a stock corporation` `a charitable nonstock corporation`
#ASSERT NOT (`May a stock corporation be merged into our charitable nonstock corporation that survives` `a stock corporation` `a nonprofit nonstock corporation that is not charitable`)

§ `Section 258: domestic with foreign stock and nonstock corporations`

-- One Delaware corporation and one foreign corporation.
#ASSERT `May our Delaware corporation merge or consolidate with a foreign corporation` 1 1 FALSE TRUE
-- The foreign law prohibits it.
#ASSERT NOT (`May our Delaware corporation merge or consolidate with a foreign corporation` 1 1 TRUE TRUE)
-- No foreign corporation takes part.
#ASSERT NOT (`May our Delaware corporation merge or consolidate with a foreign corporation` 2 0 FALSE TRUE)
-- No Delaware corporation takes part.
#ASSERT NOT (`May our Delaware corporation merge or consolidate with a foreign corporation` 0 2 FALSE TRUE)

#ASSERT `May the surviving or resulting corporation of a merger with a foreign corporation be of this kind` `a charitable nonstock corporation`

-- The agreement as section 257 provides plus what the foreign laws require.
#ASSERT `Does the merger agreement state what section 258(b) requires` FALSE TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE TRUE
-- It omits what the foreign laws require.
#ASSERT NOT (`Does the merger agreement state what section 258(b) requires` FALSE TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE)

-- A Delaware constituent: the method and procedure of section 257. A foreign constituent: its own law.
#ASSERT `Has this constituent corporation approved the agreement as section 258(b) requires` `this State` FALSE TRUE
#ASSERT NOT (`Has this constituent corporation approved the agreement as section 258(b) requires` `this State` TRUE FALSE)
#ASSERT `Has this constituent corporation approved the agreement as section 258(b) requires` `a foreign jurisdiction outside the United States` TRUE FALSE
#ASSERT NOT (`Has this constituent corporation approved the agreement as section 258(b) requires` `a foreign jurisdiction outside the United States` FALSE TRUE)

-- The survivor is foreign and a certificate of merger is filed: the appointment must be in it.
#ASSERT `Must the certificate of merger include the appointment of the Secretary of State to receive process` TRUE TRUE TRUE
#ASSERT NOT (`Must the certificate of merger include the appointment of the Secretary of State to receive process` TRUE TRUE FALSE)
-- No certificate is filed, or the survivor is not foreign: nothing to include.
#ASSERT `Must the certificate of merger include the appointment of the Secretary of State to receive process` TRUE FALSE FALSE
#ASSERT `Must the certificate of merger include the appointment of the Secretary of State to receive process` FALSE TRUE FALSE

-- Section 258 brings in s 252(d) where the survivor is a foreign corporation, and s 251(e) where it is a Delaware corporation.
#ASSERT `Does this provision of section 251 or 252 apply to our merger under section 258` `s 252(d), the appointment of the Secretary of State to receive process` TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE
#ASSERT NOT (`Does this provision of section 251 or 252 apply to our merger under section 258` `s 252(d), the appointment of the Secretary of State to receive process` TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE)
#ASSERT `Does this provision of section 251 or 252 apply to our merger under section 258` `s 251(e), the automatic amendment of the surviving corporation's certificate of incorporation` TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE
#ASSERT `Does this provision of section 251 or 252 apply to our merger under section 258` `s 251(f), no vote of the stockholders of a constituent corporation surviving a merger` TRUE TRUE FALSE TRUE

-- A charitable nonstock corporation merged into a stock corporation with its charitable status lost: not authorized by section 258.
#ASSERT `Does section 258 forbid our merger because a charitable nonstock corporation would lose its charitable status` FALSE `a charitable nonstock corporation` `a stock corporation` TRUE

§ `After the merger: ss 259 to 261`

-- My corporation was merged into the other and the merger is effective: its separate existence has ceased.
#ASSERT `Does this effect of a merger or consolidation follow for my corporation` `the separate existence of the constituent corporation ceases` TRUE FALSE
-- My corporation is the one the others were merged into: its existence goes on.
#ASSERT NOT (`Does this effect of a merger or consolidation follow for my corporation` `the separate existence of the constituent corporation ceases` TRUE TRUE)
-- The merger is not yet effective.
#ASSERT NOT (`Does this effect of a merger or consolidation follow for my corporation` `the separate existence of the constituent corporation ceases` FALSE FALSE)
-- The debts and liabilities of my corporation, merged into the other, now attach to the survivor.
#ASSERT `Does this effect of a merger or consolidation follow for my corporation` `the debts, liabilities and duties of a constituent corporation attach to the surviving or resulting corporation and may be enforced against it as if it had incurred them` TRUE FALSE
-- The creditors' liens are preserved.
#ASSERT `Does this effect of a merger or consolidation follow for my corporation` `the rights of creditors and the liens upon the property of a constituent corporation are preserved unimpaired` TRUE FALSE
-- The property of my corporation is vested in the survivor.
#ASSERT `Does this effect of a merger or consolidation follow for my corporation` `all property, debts due and things in action of each constituent corporation are vested in the surviving or resulting corporation` TRUE FALSE
-- Title to real estate does not revert, once the merger is effective; before, nothing is said.
#ASSERT `Does this effect of a merger or consolidation follow for my corporation` `title to real estate vested in a constituent corporation does not revert and is not impaired by reason of this chapter` TRUE TRUE
#ASSERT NOT (`Does this effect of a merger or consolidation follow for my corporation` `title to real estate vested in a constituent corporation does not revert and is not impaired by reason of this chapter` FALSE TRUE)

-- A merger of two trust companies is effective: the fiduciary appointments vest automatically.
#ASSERT `Do the fiduciary appointments of a merged bank or trust company vest in the surviving corporation without a court order` TRUE TRUE
-- Not a merger of banks or trust companies.
#ASSERT NOT (`Do the fiduciary appointments of a merged bank or trust company vest in the surviving corporation without a court order` FALSE TRUE)
-- A beneficiary, as a party in interest, may apply to a court for a determination.
#ASSERT `May I, as a party in interest, apply to a court or tribunal for a determination of the fiduciary` TRUE TRUE
#ASSERT NOT (`May I, as a party in interest, apply to a court or tribunal for a determination of the fiduciary` TRUE FALSE)

-- The transaction needs $5,000,000 in payments and obligations, and the capital stock is $2,000,000: up to $3,000,000 in bonds.
#ASSERT `How much may our surviving corporation issue in bonds or other obligations` 5000000 2000000 EQUALS 3000000
-- The capital stock already covers the payments: nothing may be issued under the subsection.
#ASSERT `How much may our surviving corporation issue in bonds or other obligations` 1500000 2000000 EQUALS 0
#ASSERT `May our surviving corporation issue bonds or other obligations in this amount` TRUE 3000000 5000000 2000000
#ASSERT NOT (`May our surviving corporation issue bonds or other obligations in this amount` TRUE 3000001 5000000 2000000)
#ASSERT NOT (`May our surviving corporation issue bonds or other obligations in this amount` FALSE 1000 5000000 2000000)

-- A mortgage to secure the bonds.
#ASSERT `May our surviving corporation mortgage its franchise and property to secure those bonds` TRUE
-- A mortgage for some other purpose is not within the subsection.
#ASSERT NOT (`May our surviving corporation mortgage its franchise and property to secure those bonds` FALSE)

-- Issuing shares in exchange for the constituent's shares to carry out the merger on the agreement's terms.
#ASSERT `May our surviving corporation take this action to carry out the transaction` `issue shares of its capital stock and other securities upon conversion of or in exchange for the shares, rights or securities of, or interests in, a constituent corporation, converting other entity or domesticating non-United States entity` TRUE FALSE TRUE
-- Cancelling the constituent's shares to carry out the merger.
#ASSERT `May our surviving corporation take this action to carry out the transaction` `cancel any shares, rights, securities or interests` TRUE FALSE FALSE
-- Issuing shares that are not in exchange for the constituent's interests.
#ASSERT NOT (`May our surviving corporation take this action to carry out the transaction` `issue shares of its capital stock and other securities upon conversion of or in exchange for the shares, rights or securities of, or interests in, a constituent corporation, converting other entity or domesticating non-United States entity` TRUE FALSE FALSE)
-- An action that is not to carry out the transaction.
#ASSERT NOT (`May our surviving corporation take this action to carry out the transaction` `cancel any shares, rights, securities or interests` FALSE FALSE FALSE)

-- A merger under s 251 (other than under s 251(g)) and one under s 255 may contain the section 261(a) provisions (fork F-261-1); a s 251(g) merger and a s 253 merger may not.
#ASSERT `May our merger agreement contain the provisions that section 261(a) allows` `a merger or consolidation under s 251 other than a merger under s 251(g)`
#ASSERT `May our merger agreement contain the provisions that section 261(a) allows` `a merger or consolidation under s 255`
#ASSERT NOT (`May our merger agreement contain the provisions that section 261(a) allows` `a merger under s 251(g)`)
#ASSERT NOT (`May our merger agreement contain the provisions that section 261(a) allows` `a merger of a parent corporation and its subsidiary under s 253`)

-- The other party failed to close; the s 251 agreement sets forth a break payment.
#ASSERT `Is the other party to our merger agreement subject to the penalties or consequences it sets forth` `a merger or consolidation under s 251 other than a merger under s 251(g)` TRUE FALSE FALSE TRUE
-- No failure.
#ASSERT NOT (`Is the other party to our merger agreement subject to the penalties or consequences it sets forth` `a merger or consolidation under s 251 other than a merger under s 251(g)` TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE)
-- A merger under s 257 can contain such a provision (fork F-261-1); a s 251(g) merger cannot.
#ASSERT `Is the other party to our merger agreement subject to the penalties or consequences it sets forth` `a merger or consolidation under s 257` TRUE FALSE FALSE TRUE
#ASSERT NOT (`Is the other party to our merger agreement subject to the penalties or consequences it sets forth` `a merger under s 251(g)` TRUE FALSE FALSE TRUE)

#ASSERT `May the penalties in our merger agreement include an amount based on our stockholders' lost premium` `a merger or consolidation under s 251 other than a merger under s 251(g)`
#ASSERT `May the penalties in our merger agreement include an amount based on our stockholders' lost premium` `a merger or consolidation under s 258`
#ASSERT NOT (`May the penalties in our merger agreement include an amount based on our stockholders' lost premium` `a merger under s 251(g)`)

-- We are entitled under the agreement to the payment: we may enforce it and keep it.
#ASSERT `May our corporation enforce the other party's payment obligation and keep what it pays` `a merger or consolidation under s 251 other than a merger under s 251(g)` TRUE
#ASSERT NOT (`May our corporation enforce the other party's payment obligation and keep what it pays` `a merger or consolidation under s 251 other than a merger under s 251(g)` FALSE)

-- A stockholder of a Delaware constituent, after the requisite vote, with an irrevocable appointment in the agreement.
#ASSERT `Am I, as a stockholder, bound by the stockholder representative named in the merger agreement` `a merger or consolidation under s 251 other than a merger under s 251(g)` TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE
-- Before the requisite vote.
#ASSERT NOT (`Am I, as a stockholder, bound by the stockholder representative named in the merger agreement` `a merger or consolidation under s 251 other than a merger under s 251(g)` TRUE TRUE FALSE TRUE)
-- Not a stockholder of a Delaware constituent.
#ASSERT NOT (`Am I, as a stockholder, bound by the stockholder representative named in the merger agreement` `a merger or consolidation under s 251 other than a merger under s 251(g)` TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE)

-- After the merger is effective, with consent given by the persons the agreement specifies.
#ASSERT `May the stockholder representative provision be amended` TRUE FALSE TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- The agreement forbids amendment after the merger is effective.
#ASSERT `May the stockholder representative provision be amended` TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- Before the merger is effective the paragraph says nothing about amendment.
#ASSERT `May the stockholder representative provision be amended` FALSE FALSE TRUE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING

#ASSERT `May a provision of our merger agreement under section 261(a) depend on facts outside the agreement` TRUE
#ASSERT NOT (`May a provision of our merger agreement under section 261(a) depend on facts outside the agreement` FALSE)

-- My lawsuit against the corporation was pending when it merged: it goes on as if the merger had not taken place.
#ASSERT `Is the action or proceeding I have pending prosecuted as if the merger had not taken place` TRUE TRUE
#ASSERT NOT (`Is the action or proceeding I have pending prosecuted as if the merger had not taken place` TRUE FALSE)
-- The surviving corporation may be substituted in it.
#ASSERT `May the surviving corporation be substituted in the action or proceeding I have pending` TRUE TRUE
#ASSERT NOT (`May the surviving corporation be substituted in the action or proceeding I have pending` FALSE TRUE)

§ `Appraisal rights: section 262, subsections (a), (b) and (c)`

-- A s 251 merger. My class has 150 holders of record and is not listed; the holders must take cash. Appraisal rights are available.
#ASSERT `Are appraisal rights available for my class or series of shares` `a merger or consolidation under s 251 other than a merger under s 251(g)` FALSE FALSE FALSE 150 FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE 0 FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE `any merger or consolidation in which the corporation is a constituent corporation`
-- My class is listed with 5,000 holders and the holders take only shares of the surviving corporation: the market-out removes appraisal rights.
#ASSERT NOT (`Are appraisal rights available for my class or series of shares` `a merger or consolidation under s 251 other than a merger under s 251(g)` FALSE FALSE TRUE 5000 FALSE FALSE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE 0 FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE `any merger or consolidation in which the corporation is a constituent corporation`)
-- Listed, and the holders take survivor shares plus cash for fractions of those shares: still a permitted combination.
#ASSERT NOT (`Are appraisal rights available for my class or series of shares` `a merger or consolidation under s 251 other than a merger under s 251(g)` FALSE FALSE TRUE 5000 FALSE FALSE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE 0 TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE `any merger or consolidation in which the corporation is a constituent corporation`)
-- Listed, but the holders must also take something else (cash for their shares): (b)(2) restores appraisal rights.
#ASSERT `Are appraisal rights available for my class or series of shares` `a merger or consolidation under s 251 other than a merger under s 251(g)` FALSE FALSE TRUE 5000 FALSE FALSE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE 0 FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE `any merger or consolidation in which the corporation is a constituent corporation`
-- Exactly 2,000 holders of record and not listed: not "more than 2,000", so stock for stock leaves appraisal rights available.
#ASSERT `Are appraisal rights available for my class or series of shares` `a merger or consolidation under s 251 other than a merger under s 251(g)` FALSE FALSE FALSE 2000 FALSE FALSE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE 0 FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE `any merger or consolidation in which the corporation is a constituent corporation`
-- 2,001 holders: the market-out applies.
#ASSERT NOT (`Are appraisal rights available for my class or series of shares` `a merger or consolidation under s 251 other than a merger under s 251(g)` FALSE FALSE FALSE 2001 FALSE FALSE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE 0 FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE `any merger or consolidation in which the corporation is a constituent corporation`)
-- The holders must take shares of another corporation that will be listed: permitted, so no appraisal rights for a widely held class.
#ASSERT NOT (`Are appraisal rights available for my class or series of shares` `a merger or consolidation under s 251 other than a merger under s 251(g)` FALSE FALSE TRUE 5000 FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE TRUE 10 FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE `any merger or consolidation in which the corporation is a constituent corporation`)
-- The other corporation's stock will not be listed and will have 50 holders: not a permitted item, so appraisal rights are restored.
#ASSERT `Are appraisal rights available for my class or series of shares` `a merger or consolidation under s 251 other than a merger under s 251(g)` FALSE FALSE TRUE 5000 FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE 50 FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE `any merger or consolidation in which the corporation is a constituent corporation`
-- A s 253 merger where the parent does not own all of the subsidiary's stock: paragraph (b)(3).
#ASSERT `Are appraisal rights available for my class or series of shares` `a merger of a parent corporation and its subsidiary under s 253` FALSE FALSE FALSE 50 FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE 0 FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE `any merger or consolidation in which the corporation is a constituent corporation`
-- A s 253 merger where the parent owns all of it.
#ASSERT NOT (`Are appraisal rights available for my class or series of shares` `a merger of a parent corporation and its subsidiary under s 253` FALSE FALSE FALSE 50 FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE 0 FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE `any merger or consolidation in which the corporation is a constituent corporation`)
-- A s 251(g) merger is not on the list.
#ASSERT NOT (`Are appraisal rights available for my class or series of shares` `a merger under s 251(g)` FALSE FALSE FALSE 50 FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE 0 FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE `a conversion effected pursuant to s 266`)
-- ... unless the certificate of incorporation provides appraisal rights for a merger.
#ASSERT `Are appraisal rights available for my class or series of shares` `a merger under s 251(g)` FALSE FALSE FALSE 50 FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE 0 FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE TRUE `any merger or consolidation in which the corporation is a constituent corporation`
-- The converted corporation's shares in a transaction authorized under s 265: excepted.
#ASSERT NOT (`Are appraisal rights available for my class or series of shares` `a conversion under s 266` TRUE TRUE FALSE 50 FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE 0 FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE `a conversion effected pursuant to s 266`)

-- When the transaction was approved at a meeting, the class is tested on the record date for notice of the meeting.
#ASSERT `As of what time is my class or series tested for listing and the number of holders` `approved at a meeting of stockholders` EQUALS JUST `the record date fixed to determine the stockholders entitled to receive notice of the meeting`
-- ... by written consent, on the record date for consent; under s 251(h), immediately before the agreement was signed.
#ASSERT `As of what time is my class or series tested for listing and the number of holders` `approved by consent of stockholders pursuant to s 228` EQUALS JUST `the record date fixed to determine the stockholders entitled to consent pursuant to s 228`
#ASSERT `As of what time is my class or series tested for listing and the number of holders` `approved pursuant to s 251(h)` EQUALS JUST `immediately prior to the execution of the agreement of merger under s 251(h)`
-- Not covered: a merger approved under s 253.
#ASSERT `As of what time is my class or series tested for listing and the number of holders` `approved pursuant to s 253` EQUALS NOTHING

-- I held of record, on the demand date and through the effective date, complied with subsection (d), did not vote for it or consent: entitled.
#ASSERT `Am I entitled to an appraisal of the fair value of my shares` TRUE `this State` TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE
-- I voted in favor.
#ASSERT NOT (`Am I entitled to an appraisal of the fair value of my shares` TRUE `this State` TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE)
-- I consented in writing under section 228.
#ASSERT NOT (`Am I entitled to an appraisal of the fair value of my shares` TRUE `this State` TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE TRUE)
-- I sold some shares before the effective date, so did not hold continuously.
#ASSERT NOT (`Am I entitled to an appraisal of the fair value of my shares` TRUE `this State` TRUE TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE)
-- Appraisal rights are not available for my class.
#ASSERT NOT (`Am I entitled to an appraisal of the fair value of my shares` FALSE `this State` TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE)
-- I am not the holder of record (my shares are held by a nominee): not under subsection (a).
#ASSERT NOT (`Am I entitled to an appraisal of the fair value of my shares` TRUE `this State` FALSE TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE)
-- The corporation was formed in another State.
#ASSERT NOT (`Am I entitled to an appraisal of the fair value of my shares` TRUE `another jurisdiction of the United States` TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE)

#ASSERT `Am I a stockholder for the purposes of section 262` TRUE TRUE
#ASSERT NOT (`Am I a stockholder for the purposes of section 262` FALSE TRUE)

-- My shares are held through a nominee for me: I am a beneficial owner.
#ASSERT `Am I a beneficial owner for the purposes of section 262` TRUE FALSE TRUE
#ASSERT `Am I a beneficial owner for the purposes of section 262` TRUE TRUE FALSE
#ASSERT NOT (`Am I a beneficial owner for the purposes of section 262` TRUE FALSE FALSE)
#ASSERT NOT (`Am I a beneficial owner for the purposes of section 262` FALSE TRUE FALSE)

-- An American depositary receipt: issued by a depository for stock of a corporation, deposited.
#ASSERT `Is this instrument a depository receipt for the purposes of section 262` TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE
-- Stock that is not deposited.
#ASSERT NOT (`Is this instrument a depository receipt for the purposes of section 262` TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE)

